Create a Dockerfile for a sample application, build the image, and push it to Azure Container Registry (ACR).

STEP 1: Create the Sample App and Dockerfile
STEP 2: Build the Docker Image
STEP 3: Login to Azure & Push to ACR
       i. Login to Azure
          az login
      ii. Create Azure Container Registry
          az acr create --name (NAME) \
                        --resource-group (YOUR RESOURCE) \
                        --admin-enabled true
      iii.Get ACR Login Server
          az acr show --name (REGISTRY NAME) --query loginServer --output tsv
      iv.Tag and Push Image to ACR
          docker tag (APPLICATION NAME):latest  (REGISTRY NAME).azurecr.io/(APPLICATION NAME):latest
          docker push (REGISTRY NAME).azurecr.io/(APPLICATION NAME):latest | tee acr-push-logs.txt
STEP 4:Image in ACR
      az acr repository list --name  ( REGISTRY NAME ) --output table
